{
 "note": "Get It Done 311 'Encampment' and 'Homeless Outreach' requests, counted per block by the month the request was FILED (date_requested). This is complaint volume, NOT a count of people: one encampment can generate many repeat reports, and reporting rates shift with public attention and policy pushes independently of the underlying population. Never sum with, take a ratio against, or reuse the symbology of the observed individuals/tents/vehicles counts in block_need_heatmap.geojson, which are physical street-count observations.",
 "coverage": "Requests are point-in-polygon matched to the 288 downtown block polygons. Roughly 6-7% of in-boundary requests fall between block polygons (the blocks are street segments and do not tile the full boundary) and are counted in downtown_total but not attributed to any block.",
 "caveats": {
  "basis": "Source files are grouped by closure year, so a request filed in 2022 can appear in the 2024 file. These counts are re-keyed to the month the request was FILED, which is why yearly totals differ slightly from the source files' own per-file counts.",
  "coverage": "Only requests that fall inside one of the 288 downtown block polygons are counted; roughly 6-7% of in-boundary requests land between blocks, since the blocks are street segments and do not tile the full boundary.",
  "2025": "Partial year at time of extract. Do not read as a full-year decline.",
  "start": "First encampment/outreach request in this data is 2018-08; the categories did not exist earlier."
 },
